<title>USA: Polo Ralph, others sue for infringement.</title>
<headline>Polo Ralph, others sue for infringement.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polo Ralph Lauren and other clothing and apparel manufacturers sued several small retail stores and their landlords for trademark infringement on Tuesday, said a complaint filed in the federal Southern District Court in New York.</p>
<p>Polo Ralph Lauren, Rolex Watch USA Inc, Louis Vuitton Malletier, Oakley Inc, Sara Lee Corp, Donna Karan Studio, Donna Karan International Inc, Gabrielle Studio Inc, Nautica Apparel Inc, Tommy Hilfiger Corp, Guess? Inc, Chanel Inc and Calvin Klein Inc allege in their complaint that the retail stores sell counterfeit goods.</p>
</text>
